Subject: Cantor Bounded Workspace Verification P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 6f382cab-345c-431d-a8c5-1db03d12fe49
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Bounded_Workspace_Verification_P0.sop

& [Problem]
  + isolated build targets exhausted the system volume and made otherwise-correct workspace verification fail through WSL infrastructure faults

& [Decision]
  + encode one reusable serialized verification lane with a capacity preflight and safe plan-only default

& [WhyNow]
  + the compact-session proof reproduced the operational failure during this shift
  + preventing recurrence preserves development throughput more directly than adding another inference feature atop an unstable verification surface

& [Rejected]
  + automatic cache deletion is rejected because cleanup is destructive and needs separate target inspection
  + remote build fallback is rejected because it crosses the explicitly local boundary
  + a unique target per run is rejected because it caused the measured accumulation

